{"about":"Residents (INE Census 2021) living in each IPMA warning area, by hour, under the highest level in force there (any hazard). Where people sleep, not where they are at a given hour, and never a count of people harmed. Not a warning: IPMA issues the warnings and ANEPC the instructions.","label":"hypothesis-free arithmetic on two facts: IPMA warning windows (as read) x INE census counts; Madeira zones approximated by municipality","source":"https://api.ipma.pt/open-data/forecast/warnings/warnings_www.json","sources":["https://api.ipma.pt/open-data/forecast/warnings/warnings_www.json","https://www.ine.pt/ine/json_indicador/pindica.jsp?op=2&varcd=0011609&lang=PT"],"licence":"IPMA open data (credit IPMA); INE statistics (credit INE)","read_utc":"2026-11-11T23:57:54Z","method":"For every UTC hour, an area counts under the highest level of any warning whose window overlaps that hour; its census residents are added to that level. Areas = IPMA mainland districts and Madeira zones (MCN, MCS, MPS; MRM residents are inside MCN/MCS and not counted twice). Only the warnings in IPMA's file at read time: windows already ended drop out of IPMA's file, so earlier hours come from earlier reads.","confidence":"HIGH for the arithmetic and the mainland areas; MEDIUM for Madeira (municipal approximation of IPMA zones); residents are 2021 counts.","by":"incident.datascience@web-summit.dinis","updated":"2026-11-11T23:57:54Z","peak":{"hour_utc":"2026-11-11T22:00:00Z","red":0,"orange":0,"yellow":3761935},"areas":[{"area":"LSB","name":"Lisboa","residents":2275385,"age_65_plus":489002,"hours_red":0,"hours_orange":0,"hours_yellow":5,"red_hazards":[],"orange_hazards":[],"first_red_utc":null,"last_red_utc":null},{"area":"PTO","name":"Porto","residents":1785405,"age_65_plus":375550,"hours_red":0,"hours_orange":0,"hours_yellow":21,"red_hazards":[],"orange_hazards":[],"first_red_utc":null,"last_red_utc":null},{"area":"STB","name":"Setúbal","residents":874806,"age_65_plus":198700,"hours_red":0